<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xinhai Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1911">1911</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xinhai Revolution was the revolution of 1911 that overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> and ended imperial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It was triggered by a military mutiny at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuchang">Wuchang</a> and spread rapidly as provinces declared independence. It produced the abdication of the six-year-old emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puyi">Puyi</a> on 12 February 1912 and the establishment of the Republic of China.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution.jpg" alt="Xinhai Revolution" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Opstanden,_revolutie,_SFA022823302.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
